<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Foresight AutoML report</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: {{ palette.primary }};
    --bg: {{ palette.background }};
    --bg2: {{ palette.secondary }};
    --text: {{ palette.text }};
    --warn: {{ palette.warning }};
    --dark: {{ palette.dark_blue }};
  }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);
         font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; line-height: 1.55; }
  main { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px 64px; }
  header { border-bottom: 3px solid var(--primary); padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  h1 { margin: 0; color: var(--dark); font-size: 1.8rem; }
  h2 { color: var(--dark); margin-top: 36px; font-size: 1.3rem;
       border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bg2); padding-bottom: 4px; }
  .meta { color: var(--text); opacity: 0.75; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .question { background: var(--bg2); border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
              padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .headline { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  th { background: var(--bg2); text-align: left; }
  th, td { padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bg2); vertical-align: top; }
  tr.best td { font-weight: 600; background: #EAF1FC; }
  .tag { background: var(--primary); color: #fff; border-radius: 4px;
         padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 0.75rem; margin-left: 6px; }
  .warn { border-left: 4px solid var(--warn); background: #FDF6E7;
          padding: 8px 12px; margin: 8px 0; }
  .note { background: var(--bg2); padding: 8px 12px; margin: 8px 0; }
  img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .charts img { max-width: 520px; width: 100%; }
  h3 { color: var(--dark); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 20px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .small { font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.8; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header>
  <h1>Foresight AutoML report</h1>
  <div class="meta">{{ dataset_name }} · created {{ created }}</div>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>The question</h2>
  <p class="question">{{ question }}</p>
  <p>Predicting <strong>{{ target }}</strong>: {{ problem_label }}.
  {% if positive_class is not none %}
    The model estimates the likelihood of <strong>'{{ positive_class }}'</strong>.
  {% endif %}
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How well the model does</h2>
  <p class="headline">{{ headline }}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Test result</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
    {% for row in test_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.name }}{% if row.is_selection %}<span class="tag">used to pick the model</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ row.value }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.description }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small">The test set was set aside before anything else and used exactly once,
  for this final check.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Model comparison</h2>
  <p>Each model was scored with {{ cv_folds }}-fold cross-validation on the training data
  (mean ± standard deviation across folds). The best by <strong>{{ selection_metric }}</strong>
  was <strong>{{ best_name }}</strong>.</p>
  <img alt="Model comparison chart" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ model_chart }}">
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Model</th><th>Role</th>
      {% for name in metric_names %}<th>{{ name }}</th>{% endfor %}
      <th>Seconds per fold</th></tr>
    {% for row in model_rows %}
    <tr{% if row.is_best %} class="best"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ row.name }}{% if row.is_best %}<span class="tag">best</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ row.role }}</td>
      {% if row.error %}
        <td colspan="{{ metric_names|length }}">{{ row.error }}</td>
      {% else %}
        {% for score in row.scores %}<td>{{ score }}</td>{% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
      <td>{{ row.fit_seconds }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
</section>

{% if decision %}
<section>
  <h2>Turning scores into decisions</h2>
  {% if not decision.applicable %}
  <p class="note">{{ decision.reason }}</p>
  {% else %}
  <h3>Can the probabilities be trusted?</h3>
  <p>{{ decision.calibration }}</p>
  <div class="charts">
    <img alt="Reliability chart" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ decision.reliability_chart }}">
  </div>
  <p class="small">Points close to the dashed line mean that, for example, rows given a 30%
  probability really were positive about 30% of the time.</p>

  <h3>Where to draw the line</h3>
  <p>{{ decision.costs }} {{ decision.threshold }}</p>
  <p>{{ decision.comparison }}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Strategy (test set)</th><th>Rows flagged</th><th>'{{ decision.positive_class }}' cases caught</th>
        <th>False alarms</th><th>Missed</th><th>Cost per 1,000 rows</th></tr>
    {% for row in decision.rows %}
    <tr{% if loop.first %} class="best"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ row.name }}</td><td>{{ row.flagged }}</td><td>{{ row.caught }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.false_alarms }}</td><td>{{ row.missed }}</td><td>{{ row.cost }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small">The cut-off was chosen using out-of-fold predictions on the training data;
  this table is its one check on the held-out test set. The costs are assumptions: change
  them to match the real business situation.</p>

  <h3>Who to act on first</h3>
  <div class="charts">
    <img alt="Cumulative gains chart" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ decision.gains_chart }}">
  </div>
  <ul>
    {% for line in decision.gains_lines %}<li>{{ line }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}

<section>
  <h2>What the model relies on</h2>
  <p>These are the columns the model leans on most when making predictions.
  <strong>They show what the model relies on, not what causes the outcome.</strong></p>
  <img alt="Column importance chart" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ importance_chart }}">
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Column</th><th>Share of reliance (SHAP)</th>
        <th>Score drop when shuffled</th><th>Pattern</th></tr>
    {% for row in driver_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.column }}</td><td>{{ row.share }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.perm }}</td><td>{{ row.direction }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  {% if n_used_columns > driver_rows|length %}
  <p class="small">Showing the top {{ driver_rows|length }} of {{ n_used_columns }} columns used.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="note">{{ agreement }}</p>
  {% for note in explain_notes %}<p class="warn">{{ note }}</p>{% endfor %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Data checks</h2>
  <p>{{ n_rows }} rows and {{ n_columns }} input columns:
  {{ n_train }} rows for training and {{ test_share }} ({{ n_test }} rows) held out for testing.</p>
  {% if class_rows %}
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Class</th><th>Share of training rows</th></tr>
    {% for row in class_rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.label }}</td><td>{{ row.share }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% for warning in data_warnings %}<p class="warn">{{ warning }}</p>{% endfor %}
  {% if excluded_rows %}
  <h3>Columns not used</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Column</th><th>Why</th></tr>
    {% for row in excluded_rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.column }}</td><td>{{ row.reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in caveats %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Method</h2>
  <ul class="small">
    <li>{{ test_share }} of rows held out (stratified for classification), random seed {{ seed }}.</li>
    <li>All preprocessing (filling missing values, scaling, encoding) was learned inside
        each cross-validation training fold only.</li>
    <li>{{ cv_folds }}-fold cross-validation for model comparison; the test set was used once.</li>
    {% if decision and decision.applicable %}
    <li>Calibration and the cut-off were chosen on out-of-fold predictions for the training
        data (calibration nested inside each fold), then checked once on the test set.</li>
    {% endif %}
    <li>SHAP values on {{ shap_rows }} test rows; permutation importance on {{ perm_rows }} test rows,
        {{ perm_repeats }} repeats, measured as the drop in {{ perm_metric }}.</li>
    <li>Total run time {{ runtime }} seconds. {{ versions }}.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

</main>
</body>
</html>
